In fact, I'm so sure of it.

1404
01:10:21,370 --> 01:10:22,130
No, wait, wait, wait.

1405
01:10:22,290 --> 01:10:23,150
What about Valentina?

1406
01:10:23,830 --> 01:10:24,930
I forgot about Valentina.

1407
01:10:25,070 --> 01:10:25,250
Fuck.

1408
01:10:26,770 --> 01:10:28,470
Maybe we don't need her for this.

1409
01:10:29,070 --> 01:10:30,130
Okay, check this out.

1410
01:10:30,270 --> 01:10:30,690
What if...

1411
01:10:30,690 --> 01:10:31,190
What if...

1412
01:10:31,830 --> 01:10:33,530
What if we go rescue Valentina...

1413
01:10:34,250 --> 01:10:35,930
And in the same mission...

1414
01:10:35,930 --> 01:10:37,190
Go straight to the moon?

1415
01:10:39,110 --> 01:10:40,890
Okay, maybe that's a little too crazy, actually.

1416
01:10:41,550 --> 01:10:42,930
It sounds fun, but...

1417
01:10:43,350 --> 01:10:44,870
Let's not go too wild.

1418
01:10:46,230 --> 01:10:47,570
That's maybe a little crazy.

1419
01:10:48,070 --> 01:10:49,670
We have enough data on the moon.

1420
01:10:49,790 --> 01:10:50,210
Oh, wait a minute.

1421
01:10:51,210 --> 01:10:52,750
There's also other moons.

1422
01:10:52,750 --> 01:10:52,890
Moons.

1423
01:10:54,750 --> 01:10:55,110
Right?

1424
01:10:56,270 --> 01:10:57,150
There's a moon here!

1425
01:10:57,890 --> 01:10:59,270
We could check that out, too.

1426
01:11:00,890 --> 01:11:02,250
It's at a bit of an inclination.

1427
01:11:03,670 --> 01:11:05,550
We could do either, actually.

1428
01:11:06,090 --> 01:11:08,650
And if we get here, and we just do like a...

1429
01:11:09,370 --> 01:11:13,190
Like an orbit or whatever, a flyby, and do science, we're going to get a lot of science, probably.

1430
01:11:13,310 --> 01:11:13,410
Right?

1431
01:11:15,230 --> 01:11:17,030
This may actually be a better idea.

1432
01:11:19,730 --> 01:11:21,090
Or we go even further.

1433
01:11:22,630 --> 01:11:23,450
Oh, my gosh.

1434
01:11:25,890 --> 01:11:26,290
Damn.

1435
01:11:31,090 --> 01:11:32,070
I'm so excited.

1436
01:11:33,470 --> 01:11:34,430
I really am.

1437
01:11:35,690 --> 01:11:36,090
Okay.

1438
01:11:37,590 --> 01:11:38,990
Let's start with the moon, shall we?

1439
01:11:39,290 --> 01:11:39,850
I mean...

1440
01:11:39,850 --> 01:11:41,510
It feels like the right progression, you know?

1441
01:11:41,550 --> 01:11:43,130
To go moon, and then to the next one.

1442
01:11:43,130 --> 01:11:47,390
But I guess they're both kind of part of the Kerbin system.

1443
01:11:49,030 --> 01:11:49,330
Also, what?

1444
01:11:50,150 --> 01:11:50,590
So...

1445
01:11:53,070 --> 01:11:53,810
Carson's debris.

1446
01:11:56,410 --> 01:11:57,770
What am I going to do with this?

1447
01:12:03,180 --> 01:12:04,740
How would I ever de-orbit this?

1448
01:12:04,860 --> 01:12:06,320
I guess I would somehow...

1449
01:12:06,840 --> 01:12:11,800
Get up there, bring a rocket up to it, and somehow attach it to the rocket, and then...

1450
01:12:11,800 --> 01:12:13,040
Do a de-orbit burn?

1451
01:12:14,000 --> 01:12:14,700
Or what?

1452
01:12:16,460 --> 01:12:16,860
What?

1453
01:12:16,860 --> 01:12:18,280
This is the one with Valentina.

1454
01:12:18,860 --> 01:12:19,580
What is that?

1455
01:12:21,020 --> 01:12:21,420
Terminate.

1456
01:12:21,620 --> 01:12:22,480
Oh, maybe I can just...

1457
01:12:22,480 --> 01:12:23,140
Terminate.

1458
01:12:26,960 --> 01:12:29,300
This will destroy the vessel, killing all crew in it.

1459
01:12:29,380 --> 01:12:30,260
Are you sure you want to continue?

1460
01:12:31,300 --> 01:12:32,380
But there's nobody in it.

1461
01:12:33,280 --> 01:12:34,760
Will it say the same thing on all?

1462
01:12:35,300 --> 01:12:35,700
Okay.

1463
01:12:36,840 --> 01:12:37,940
Ah, alright, there we go.

1464
01:12:38,820 --> 01:12:40,600
Clean up the freaking space debris.

1465
01:12:41,720 --> 01:12:42,760
Why can't I...

1466
01:12:42,760 --> 01:12:43,300
Oh, there we go.

1467
01:12:44,760 --> 01:12:45,160
Beautiful.

1468
01:12:45,760 --> 01:12:46,940
Can I rename this?

1469
01:12:48,400 --> 01:12:48,800
Somehow.

1470
01:12:51,500 --> 01:12:52,100
Maybe not.

1471
01:12:57,530 --> 01:12:57,930
Ah.

1472
01:12:58,330 --> 01:12:58,730
Okay.

1473
01:13:01,780 --> 01:13:02,580
Well, that's better.

1474
01:13:02,780 --> 01:13:04,600
It's going to be much easier now to see what's going on.

1475
01:13:05,600 --> 01:13:07,740
Guys, I think we got to go rescue Valentina first.

1476
01:13:08,180 --> 01:13:09,800
The crew has one more mission.

1477
01:13:10,160 --> 01:13:10,900
The crew too.

1478
01:13:11,120 --> 01:13:11,680
I mean.

1479
01:13:13,160 --> 01:13:14,260
And maybe we...

1480
01:13:14,260 --> 01:13:15,300
Oh, Sherlock was an engineer.

1481
01:13:15,460 --> 01:13:15,700
Interesting.

1482
01:13:15,880 --> 01:13:16,720
And he has one star.

1483
01:13:17,000 --> 01:13:17,900
So look at this now.

1484
01:13:19,220 --> 01:13:20,700
Provides repair skills.

1485
01:13:21,260 --> 01:13:22,680
Repack parachutes?

1486
01:13:24,540 --> 01:13:26,520
Engineer can repair failures.

1487
01:13:27,120 --> 01:13:28,900
Deploy power generation units.

1488
01:13:29,560 --> 01:13:30,180
What?

1489
01:13:30,480 --> 01:13:32,060
I'm so confused by all that.

1490
01:13:32,660 --> 01:13:34,440
But it's cool, I guess.

1491
01:13:37,180 --> 01:13:39,200
Wait, Carson is our only pilot.

1492
01:13:40,000 --> 01:13:42,080
We kind of need Valentina then.

1493
01:13:42,440 --> 01:13:43,520
Like, no question about it.

1494
01:13:45,560 --> 01:13:47,140
Let me quickly see where she is.

1495
01:13:47,760 --> 01:13:49,480
Because we should wait for her to come by again.

1496
01:13:49,680 --> 01:13:51,000
This is like, the way to do it.

1497
01:13:53,800 --> 01:13:56,020
We're doing rescue missions back to back here.

1498
01:13:57,820 --> 01:13:58,860
Okay, you're right there.

1499
01:14:00,640 --> 01:14:02,340
I guess I can wait for you to take a trip around.

1500
01:14:02,460 --> 01:14:03,600
It's like 20 minutes or so, right?

1501
01:14:04,700 --> 01:14:05,560
Actually, less maybe.

1502
01:14:06,520 --> 01:14:07,920
It's like 15 minutes-ish?

1503
01:14:11,400 --> 01:14:11,920
Wee!

1504
01:14:12,060 --> 01:14:12,940
Oh, don't go too fast.

1505
01:14:14,440 --> 01:14:16,020
I hope Valentina isn't starving.

1506
01:14:18,320 --> 01:14:20,000
Okay, so she's here now-ish.

1507
01:14:22,060 --> 01:14:22,580
Now.

1508
01:14:25,510 --> 01:14:26,270
Here I come!

1509
01:14:28,790 --> 01:14:30,330
Uh, here.

1510
01:14:32,830 --> 01:14:33,670
And then...

1511
01:14:33,670 --> 01:14:34,470
Let me just double-check.

1512
01:14:35,350 --> 01:14:35,770
Yes.

1513
01:14:36,330 --> 01:14:36,750
Carson.

1514
01:14:37,430 --> 01:14:38,730
That one, these two.

1515
01:14:38,990 --> 01:14:40,370
That one, this one.

1516
01:14:41,430 --> 01:14:43,510
Dude, we don't even need all this delta-V, actually.

1517
01:14:43,710 --> 01:14:45,070
We can even- we can calm down a bit.

1518
01:14:45,670 --> 01:14:47,510
We had way more than we needed last time.

1519
01:14:47,830 --> 01:14:48,930
Let's not go too crazy.

1520
01:14:52,470 --> 01:14:53,290
That's all we need.

1521
01:14:54,090 --> 01:14:54,510
Boom.

1522
01:14:56,010 --> 01:14:56,610
Hell yeah.

1523
01:14:58,150 --> 01:14:58,610
Let's go.

1524
01:15:00,150 --> 01:15:00,750
Cheers.

1525
01:15:09,200 --> 01:15:09,800
Carson!

1526
01:15:10,660 --> 01:15:11,780
Lift off again!

1527
01:15:12,440 --> 01:15:14,860
We are going to get Valentina.

1528
01:15:15,460 --> 01:15:16,640
Let's see where she is.

1529
01:15:17,660 --> 01:15:18,960
She's coming right there.

1530
01:15:19,560 --> 01:15:21,260
This is so fucking sick!

1531
01:15:21,820 --> 01:15:23,560
Dude, I love the rescue mission!

1532
01:15:24,140 --> 01:15:25,260
It's so dope.

1533
01:15:26,420 --> 01:15:27,300
Very nice.

1534
01:15:28,880 --> 01:15:31,120
Also, I forgot how much this rocket is worth.

1535
01:15:31,540 --> 01:15:33,240
Maybe it's like 10,000 or so?

1536
01:15:33,240 --> 01:15:38,140
Well, that's definitely, uh, less than what Valentina's worth, right?

1537
01:15:38,820 --> 01:15:40,520
In fact, I'm gonna slightly turn if I can.

1538
01:15:40,820 --> 01:15:41,500
Looks like I can.

1539
01:15:42,560 --> 01:15:43,000
Slightly.

1540
01:15:45,380 --> 01:15:47,340
Hey, I'm surprised I can turn this much already.

1541
01:15:49,280 --> 01:15:50,320
I wonder why that is.

1542
01:15:50,460 --> 01:15:51,640
Maybe it's because I'm moving a little slower.

1543
01:15:55,680 --> 01:15:56,980
So in time to separate.

1544
01:15:57,520 --> 01:15:57,960
Stages.

1545
01:16:00,800 --> 01:16:01,900
Carson is loving it.

1546
01:16:03,120 --> 01:16:04,800
Kind of wish you could give these guys haircuts.

1547
01:16:06,080 --> 01:16:07,900
I would love Carson to have, like, a mohawk.

1548
01:16:09,960 --> 01:16:10,320
Imagine.

1549
01:16:11,200 --> 01:16:12,760
Or put glasses on them or something.

1550
01:16:16,570 --> 01:16:17,930
Okay, now we start turning even more.

1551
01:16:17,930 --> 01:16:18,770
I'm getting better at this, dude.

1552
01:16:19,490 --> 01:16:21,090
Also, let me see the orbital parameters.

1553
01:16:22,730 --> 01:16:23,450
Looking good.

1554
01:16:23,890 --> 01:16:25,330
I need to see which height she's at.

1555
01:16:26,890 --> 01:16:27,550
Almost a hundred.

1556
01:16:28,210 --> 01:16:29,010
A hundred kilometers.

1557
01:16:31,110 --> 01:16:31,710
That's cool.

1558
01:16:34,210 --> 01:16:35,890
We can go a little more horizontal here.

1559
01:16:38,650 --> 01:16:40,190
In fact, we can go very horizontal.

1560
01:16:43,220 --> 01:16:46,100
I love the way you can see the gimbal of the engine, too, when I steer it.

1561
01:16:46,600 --> 01:16:47,460
It's a nice detail.

1562
01:16:56,810 --> 01:16:57,550
Here I come.

1563
01:16:57,710 --> 01:16:59,150
I should actually slow down.

1564
01:17:00,650 --> 01:17:02,270
Or not go as high yet.

1565
01:17:05,740 --> 01:17:08,540
I want to stay a little below her so I can potentially catch up to her.

1566
01:17:08,600 --> 01:17:09,140
She's ahead of me.

1567
01:17:16,500 --> 01:17:18,720
Oh, we're going a little too high.

1568
01:17:18,920 --> 01:17:20,380
I'm going to try and bring it down just slightly.

1569
01:17:20,480 --> 01:17:22,200
It looks weird, the angle, but...

1570
01:17:22,200 --> 01:17:23,260
I think it's fine.

1571
01:17:26,370 --> 01:17:27,550
I'm looking at this number here.

1572
01:17:29,290 --> 01:17:29,610
Apoapses.

1573
01:17:30,850 --> 01:17:32,610
Okay, we're going to run out of fuel here in a sec.

1574
01:17:32,670 --> 01:17:32,970
Oh, god.

1575
01:17:33,130 --> 01:17:33,850
Slow down even more.

1576
01:17:35,150 --> 01:17:35,750
Further down.

1577
01:17:39,840 --> 01:17:41,160
Just stay below her orbit.

1578
01:17:41,340 --> 01:17:42,140
That's all I want right now.

1579
01:17:42,920 --> 01:17:43,360
Okay, good.

1580
01:17:47,360 --> 01:17:48,680
Oh, we're a little far behind.

1581
01:17:51,640 --> 01:17:52,440
87 meters.

1582
01:17:52,800 --> 01:17:53,860
87,000 meters.

1583
01:17:54,420 --> 01:17:55,480
So, we're at...

1584
01:17:55,480 --> 01:17:56,160
Oh, we're at 1,900.

1585
01:17:57,260 --> 01:17:58,580
We don't need a lot here.

1586
01:17:59,460 --> 01:18:00,780
This is going to be quite fast.

1587
01:18:01,560 --> 01:18:02,880
So, let's burn in...

1588
01:18:04,240 --> 01:18:04,740
Oh, god.

1589
01:18:04,800 --> 01:18:05,320
Let me estimate.

1590
01:18:05,500 --> 01:18:06,380
This is going to take...

1591
01:18:07,080 --> 01:18:09,280
It's going to take 20...

1592
01:18:09,280 --> 01:18:09,980
30 seconds.

1593
01:18:11,480 --> 01:18:12,240
25 seconds.

1594
01:18:13,760 --> 01:18:16,940
That means we're going to start burning when this is like 12-ish seconds.

1595
01:18:17,540 --> 01:18:18,800
I'm going to fast forward slightly.

1596
01:18:26,730 --> 01:18:27,450
Get ready.

1597
01:18:30,690 --> 01:18:31,390
There we go.

1598
01:18:35,740 --> 01:18:36,200
Valentina!

1599
01:18:38,100 --> 01:18:46,280
By the way, I definitely took notice now that we need to have the vessel that we're trying to reach be a little further behind than what I had it here.

1600
01:19:00,780 --> 01:19:01,400
Looks good.

1601
01:19:03,080 --> 01:19:03,480
Target.

1602
01:19:09,650 --> 01:19:10,230
Oh, wait.

1603
01:19:10,310 --> 01:19:11,630
The inclination is a little off here.

1604
01:19:16,060 --> 01:19:18,160
Let me see exactly where it differs.

1605
01:19:19,540 --> 01:19:20,940
It's like right here, right?

1606
01:19:21,140 --> 01:19:21,880
It's like there.

1607
01:19:22,080 --> 01:19:23,240
Actually, it's right at periapsis.

1608
01:19:26,210 --> 01:19:33,090
So, if I want to change that, I want to burn up over here to bring that up there, which is going to bring this down.

1609
01:19:35,130 --> 01:19:35,910
What is up?

1610
01:19:39,780 --> 01:19:41,260
Wait, this is the way I'm facing now.

1611
01:19:43,500 --> 01:19:43,820
Nope.

1612
01:19:43,960 --> 01:19:44,320
Wrong one.

1613
01:19:46,540 --> 01:19:47,140
There we go.

1614
01:19:48,480 --> 01:19:50,020
Oh, I guess that's what that means then.

1615
01:19:50,140 --> 01:19:50,780
It's like normal.

1616
01:19:51,640 --> 01:19:52,860
To the velocity vector.

1617
01:19:54,460 --> 01:19:55,380
Right-hand rule.

1618
01:20:01,420 --> 01:20:02,540
Okay, so let's wait a bit.

1619
01:20:06,620 --> 01:20:07,840
This looks about right.

1620
01:20:17,910 --> 01:20:18,590
Pretty good.

1621
01:20:23,490 --> 01:20:27,410
But now we need to find out how to actually get to catch up to her.

1622
01:20:28,130 --> 01:20:30,050
We actually have kind of an encounter here.

1623
01:20:32,130 --> 01:20:32,610
Hmm.

1624
01:20:32,890 --> 01:20:34,410
We're a little too far out here.

1625
01:20:35,150 --> 01:20:36,970
Kind of want to burn retrograde right now.

1626
01:20:41,560 --> 01:20:44,420
Which means I'm going to bring apwapsis down slightly.

1627
01:20:49,690 --> 01:20:51,090
Which means we're going to catch up.

1628
01:21:00,720 --> 01:21:02,100
Burning very slowly here.

1629
01:21:05,950 --> 01:21:06,350
Beautiful.

1630
01:21:07,110 --> 01:21:08,070
The question is...

1631
01:21:08,070 --> 01:21:09,270
Ah, we're still below the atmosphere.

1632
01:21:09,270 --> 01:21:11,930
I burned a little too much, but, you know, it's better than 52.

1633
01:21:12,410 --> 01:21:13,870
Last time I was at 52.

1634
01:21:14,430 --> 01:21:14,650
Haha.

1635
01:21:15,310 --> 01:21:16,330
This is going to be much easier.

1636
01:21:21,390 --> 01:21:25,530
So, basically, you want to be in a lower orbit than the one you're trying to get up to.

1637
01:21:26,190 --> 01:21:27,510
Because then you move faster, right?

1638
01:21:29,110 --> 01:21:30,850
This is why we're catching up to him now.

1639
01:21:31,690 --> 01:21:32,530
Or her, I mean.

1640
01:21:33,610 --> 01:21:35,090
Okay, so I think we just entered atmosphere.

1641
01:21:36,150 --> 01:21:37,470
We're not going to speed up a lot.

1642
01:21:37,710 --> 01:21:38,910
I mean, slow down a lot.

1643
01:21:39,370 --> 01:21:40,630
It's going to be very slight.

1644
01:21:45,860 --> 01:21:46,940
Actually, you know what I think?

1645
01:21:47,680 --> 01:21:55,860
Instead of trying to get into an orbit that is lower than the target, maybe it just, in general, makes more sense to go into a higher orbit.

1646
01:21:57,020 --> 01:22:04,200
Because that way, you're not going to have the atmosphere problem, and you're just going to let them catch up to you, instead of me catching up to them like I'm doing now.

1647
01:22:06,120 --> 01:22:06,480
Yeah.

1648
01:22:06,720 --> 01:22:07,660
Actually, that makes so much sense.

1649
01:22:07,720 --> 01:22:08,400
Let's do that next time.

1650
01:22:09,940 --> 01:22:10,980
That makes a lot of sense.

1651
01:22:12,280 --> 01:22:13,720
It's now 32 kilometers.

1652
01:22:13,720 --> 01:22:15,740
I feel like we should do that.

1653
01:22:15,940 --> 01:22:16,000
Yeah.

1654
01:22:19,760 --> 01:22:21,820
It's changing a lot, because we're moving through the atmosphere.

1655
01:22:21,820 --> 01:22:22,760
We're slowing down.

1656
01:22:23,000 --> 01:22:25,040
But it doesn't look like we're slowing down, but we kind of are.

1657
01:22:25,220 --> 01:22:26,020
We're bleeding off energy.

1658
01:22:26,600 --> 01:22:31,320
The reason why we're bleeding off, or it looks like we're still speeding up, is because we're moving towards periapsis.

1659
01:22:36,460 --> 01:22:36,860
Okay.

1660
01:22:38,280 --> 01:22:39,200
Plenty of fuel, man.

1661
01:22:39,220 --> 01:22:40,180
This is an easy one.

1662
01:22:40,260 --> 01:22:41,700
We got this one in the bag, homie.

1663
01:22:43,440 --> 01:22:45,660
Valentina can finally come home and eat lunch.

1664
01:22:46,020 --> 01:22:47,100
She must be starving.

1665
01:22:48,520 --> 01:22:49,860
I wonder how long she's been up here.

1666
01:22:49,940 --> 01:22:51,700
Can I, like, see a mission time on this vessel?

1667
01:22:52,500 --> 01:22:53,960
Maybe I can do it from the tracking center.

1668
01:22:57,700 --> 01:22:58,560
In fact, hold on.

1669
01:22:59,640 --> 01:23:00,540
I can do that right now.

1670
01:23:02,760 --> 01:23:03,340
Switch two.

