05:01:13,370 --> 05:01:14,530
There's like a million buttons.

6114
05:01:17,730 --> 05:01:21,970
It looks a little too realistic for the silliness that is the Kerbal universe, doesn't it?

6115
05:01:23,810 --> 05:01:25,770
It's all the usual instruments, but in IV-V-A.

6116
05:01:25,870 --> 05:01:26,410
Oh, okay.

6117
05:01:27,210 --> 05:01:28,730
Okay, hold on, you have my attention.

6118
05:01:31,840 --> 05:01:32,940
Okay, I'll write it on the list.

6119
05:01:33,040 --> 05:01:34,120
I'll check it out, I'll check it out.

6120
05:01:36,680 --> 05:01:38,460
Wait, I need to just copy the name here.

6121
05:01:42,960 --> 05:01:46,420
Guys, I need to ask, what was your reaction to, uh...

6122
05:01:46,420 --> 05:01:50,160
What did you think of my attempt at trying to rescue Valentina today?

6123
05:01:51,920 --> 05:01:55,640
Because that was like a car crash in slow motion at this point.

6124
05:01:57,060 --> 05:01:58,100
Wasn't that crazy?

6125
05:01:59,200 --> 05:02:01,660
I can't believe we lost Valentina, man.

6126
05:02:03,060 --> 05:02:04,680
Oh, it was so bad.

6127
05:02:06,440 --> 05:02:09,040
You pointed it prograde when it was already retro?

6128
05:02:09,240 --> 05:02:10,200
Nah, no, no, no.

6129
05:02:11,040 --> 05:02:11,520
Nope.

6130
05:02:11,920 --> 05:02:12,680
I didn't.

6131
05:02:14,280 --> 05:02:15,920
I am 100% sure I didn't.

6132
05:02:17,120 --> 05:02:22,260
Because you have to remember, it's going to stay the same orientation going around Kerban.

6133
05:02:23,160 --> 05:02:23,660
Right?

6134
05:02:24,740 --> 05:02:29,440
So if it was retro on one side, it's not going to be retro on the other side.

6135
05:02:35,160 --> 05:02:36,620
You did exactly 180?

6136
05:02:37,620 --> 05:02:38,540
Well, exactly.

6137
05:02:38,720 --> 05:02:39,380
That's the point.

6138
05:02:40,120 --> 05:02:41,480
I wanted to do 180.

6139
05:02:43,100 --> 05:02:44,840
Unless you meant to say 360 just now.

6140
05:02:47,400 --> 05:02:47,720
Yeah.

6141
05:02:48,260 --> 05:02:50,100
I mean, in hindsight, I knew what I should have done.

6142
05:02:50,220 --> 05:02:50,960
I even thought about it.

6143
05:02:51,020 --> 05:02:51,760
I even said it out loud.

6144
05:02:52,160 --> 05:02:56,160
What I should have done was try to get into a stable orbit with just my Kerbal.

6145
05:02:56,680 --> 05:02:57,560
Using my thrusters.

6146
05:02:58,160 --> 05:02:59,860
Because you actually have some power in those.

6147
05:03:00,380 --> 05:03:03,020
I mean, you can get up to quite a bit of meters per second with that.

6148
05:03:03,700 --> 05:03:06,420
So all I should have done is just go into a stable orbit with her.

6149
05:03:06,720 --> 05:03:08,640
And then come rescue her later.

6150
05:03:09,260 --> 05:03:10,380
I even thought about it.

6151
05:03:10,460 --> 05:03:12,580
But I fucking hubris took over, man.

6152
05:03:12,680 --> 05:03:13,880
I thought I had it.

6153
05:03:14,700 --> 05:03:16,520
And I thought it was such a cool attempt, you know?

6154
05:03:17,180 --> 05:03:18,460
I wanted to go for it.

6155
05:03:19,340 --> 05:03:20,920
That's the Valentina way, man.

6156
05:03:21,020 --> 05:03:22,280
She's a brave old Kerbal.

6157
05:03:23,620 --> 05:03:25,020
What's the mod for Parachute Physics?

6158
05:03:25,080 --> 05:03:25,940
That's part of my own mod.

6159
05:03:28,380 --> 05:03:29,680
I just call it my tweaks.

6160
05:03:30,100 --> 05:03:31,660
Add some funny little things, you know?

6161
05:03:38,720 --> 05:03:42,940
If you had completely burned through the remaining step, you would have had enough electricity for SAS.

6162
05:03:43,820 --> 05:03:45,760
Yeah, I realized later on, right?

6163
05:03:45,860 --> 05:03:46,640
That that was...

6164
05:03:46,640 --> 05:03:47,880
I mean, I didn't really know at the time.

6165
05:03:48,080 --> 05:03:49,280
You have to remember, like...

6166
05:03:49,700 --> 05:03:53,100
I didn't realize that was what was happening at the time.

6167
05:03:59,460 --> 05:04:00,540
Yeah, it's fully custom.

6168
05:04:00,680 --> 05:04:09,860
It's just asking Opus 5.5, Hey, make it, like, fold and, you know, bend with the wind and have it, you know, fall down realistically.

6169
05:04:10,060 --> 05:04:10,180
Boom.

6170
05:04:10,320 --> 05:04:10,480
Done.

6171
05:04:11,140 --> 05:04:11,960
So awesome, man.

6172
05:04:12,020 --> 05:04:15,600
We're entering an age where you just do amazing things with your games, you know?

6173
05:04:16,100 --> 05:04:16,840
I love it.

6174
05:04:18,020 --> 05:04:19,120
Do you have community fixes?

6175
05:04:19,240 --> 05:04:19,640
I do.

6176
05:04:20,060 --> 05:04:20,900
I do have it.

6177
05:04:23,040 --> 05:04:25,720
I'm not sure what it fixes, but I like something being fixed.

6178
05:04:27,140 --> 05:04:27,920
So I have it.

6179
05:04:32,330 --> 05:04:36,290
I think time warping on the moon with your SAS still on is what drained the battery.

6180
05:04:37,270 --> 05:04:40,550
Oh, yeah, because I was constantly adjusting all the time.

6181
05:04:40,710 --> 05:04:41,190
It makes sense.

6182
05:04:41,890 --> 05:04:43,310
I mean, that's what I thought as well, you know?

6183
05:04:43,370 --> 05:04:44,070
I had it on too much.

6184
05:04:44,090 --> 05:04:44,930
I was using it too much.

6185
05:04:49,410 --> 05:04:51,110
Okay, guys, it's time for me to eat.

6186
05:04:52,410 --> 05:04:53,210
I am hungry.

6187
05:04:54,270 --> 05:04:55,210
Thank you for watching.

6188
05:04:55,530 --> 05:04:56,570
This was a great stream.

6189
05:04:57,690 --> 05:04:59,410
As always, this game is, like...

6190
05:04:59,410 --> 05:05:01,350
This series may become one of my favorites I've done.

6191
05:05:01,450 --> 05:05:01,990
I'm not even kidding.

6192
05:05:02,580 --> 05:05:04,050
Like, if this keeps up...

6193
05:05:04,050 --> 05:05:04,830
Holy shit.

6194
05:05:06,430 --> 05:05:08,150
Fucking 10 out of 10 so far on this.

6195
05:05:08,570 --> 05:05:08,790
Damn.

6196
05:05:09,670 --> 05:05:10,570
I'll see you around.

6197
05:05:11,570 --> 05:05:12,610
Thanks for sticking around.

6198
05:05:12,890 --> 05:05:13,090
Bye-bye.
